flowchart LR
    accTitle: Strategy One - intent routing and concurrent execution
    accDescr: Chat is classified before a response or action request. A mailbox feeds events to the agent. The agent edits a FIFO queue; the executor runs one action at a time and posts completion results back to the mailbox. Model generation and physical execution can overlap.
    U["Player chat"] --> R{"Intent"}
    R -->|"Question"| C["Chat reply"]
    R -->|"Action"| M["Mailbox<br/>messages + results"]
    M --> L["LLM decision"]
    L -->|"Queue / resume"| Q["FIFO queue<br/>1. goto<br/>2. equip<br/>3. dig"]
    Q -->|"Next action"| E["Execute one action<br/>via Mineflayer"]
    E -->|"Result"| M
    L -.->|"Concurrent"| E
